# What not to put on GitHub.
#
# Drop this file at the top of your course repository, beside README.md.
# Git reads it and leaves everything listed here out of your commits.

# The virtual environment. Hundreds of megabytes, rebuilt by `uv sync`
# from pyproject.toml and uv.lock, so it never belongs in a repository.
.venv/

# marimo writes the outputs of every cell here while you work, as one large
# JSON file per notebook. Your .py notebook stays clean because of it, which
# is the point. Commit it and you get a file that changes every time you run
# anything, and it carries whatever your cells printed.
__marimo__/
.marimo.toml

# Python's compiled bytecode. Regenerated on every run.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# API keys and anything else private. Your repository is public.
.env

# macOS folder metadata.
.DS_Store
__marimo__/
